yoyo no longer suggests the three dead Claude ids. Commit a5970942 is local and goes out with this session's push. Build, the full test suite, clippy, fmt and tests/harness_logic.sh all pass.

What changed
• Lists: claude-sonnet-4-5 (including its dated Bedrock spelling), claude-sonnet-4-7 and claude-sonnet-4-20250514 are gone from the anthropic and bedrock known-model lists in src/providers.rs and from the /model completions in src/commands.rs. Price rows are unchanged, so anyone still on 4.5 keeps getting cost estimates until Nov 30.
• Default first: the anthropic list was missing the default, claude-opus-5-5, along with claude-sonnet-5-5 and claude-haiku-5-5. All three are in now, with the default first. That matters because the 404 hint's "Switch with" line uses the first entry, which until now was claude-opus-5. The bedrock default, anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6, now leads its list too.
• Beyond the planned files: claude-sonnet-4-20250514 was also the example model in the no-key banner, the --help config example, two help topics and four docs pages. Those now say claude-sonnet-5-5.

New tests in src/anthropic_preset_tests.rs:
• Every offered Claude id must exist in yoagent: either as a preset or as a row in its built-in anthropic price table. The test also checks that the three dead ids and anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-7 fail this, so it would have caught them. Every id still on the lists passes; I removed none that I hadn't checked.
• The task suggested ModelConfig::anthropic(id) as a fallback check, but it can't do that job: it works out limits for any claude-X-Y name, including the nonexistent claude-sonnet-4-7.
• Two more tests: none of the dead ids appears anywhere offered (with claude-sonnet-4-6 as the close-but-valid case), and the default comes first in both lists.

Existing tests I edited:
• Tests that asserted the dead ids are offered now assert they aren't. One was renamed because its name said "contains".
• The test that pins the exact "Unknown model" warning text now expects the new first five ids.
• A pricing-audit test needed ids that are priced but not on the list. It used claude-opus-5-5 and claude-haiku-5-5, which are listed now, so it uses claude-opus-4-5 and claude-fable-5-1 instead.

Check: --model claude-sonnet-4-7 -p hi with a fake key now prints Unknown model 'claude-sonnet-4-7' … Known models: claude-opus-5-5, claude-sonnet-5-5, claude-haiku-5-5, claude-opus-5, claude-fable-5. Before, the id was on the list and nothing warned. The fake key stopped the run at a 401, so I couldn't reach the 404 hint's "Available models" list. The grep for claude-sonnet-4-7 in src/providers.rs and src/commands.rs returns 0.

Issue comments: I commented on #1144 now rather than after the push, since the harness does the push; the comment says the commit lands with it. Item 3 is done; items 1 and 2 are still open. I also noted that claude-sonnet-4-5 still appears in pricing code and as test inputs, which I deliberately left alone. On #1121 I listed the three removed bedrock rows and flagged an open problem: anthropic.claude-opus-4-7 passes the new test only through the anthropic price table. yoagent has no Bedrock mapping for it, so it may still run on guessed limits, and I haven't checked that Bedrock id against AWS's model cards.
